        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e084e818-dbc5-32dc-a2ad-eeaae604e007",
                "word": "verjus",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1c3658b-28eb-3844-8cac-5d02d87595fb",
                        "entry_id": "e084e818-dbc5-32dc-a2ad-eeaae604e007",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Suc acide qu’on tire des raisins qui ne sont pas mûrs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2d17d01-52c3-4bc1-855d-0afef2653bbc",
                                "sense_id": "e1c3658b-28eb-3844-8cac-5d02d87595fb",
                                "text": "Il est le plus souvent rôti et mangé à la dodine; cette sauce, prescrite pour les oiseaux de rivière, est un déglaçage du jus de cuisson à l’aide de lait, de vin ou de verjus épicé au gingembre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d81a7140-c5bc-3ed5-a4a0-344aabb884c8",
                        "entry_id": "e084e818-dbc5-32dc-a2ad-eeaae604e007",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vin qui est trop vert."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ffb561ef-c454-462a-a704-f96e96f1edbf",
                                "sense_id": "d81a7140-c5bc-3ed5-a4a0-344aabb884c8",
                                "text": "Et quand en 1840, notre vin de Moselle ne fut qu’un âpre verjus, nos vignerons, par dérision et par haine du Prussien, donnèrent sarcastiquement à ce vin imbuvable le sobriquet de : Hassenpflug."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d2ab731-0706-3b39-9848-b03d31064ca1",
                        "entry_id": "e084e818-dbc5-32dc-a2ad-eeaae604e007",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Raisin qu’on cueille encore vert."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "969b70d4-73a2-47f0-9aab-5f9c14cea9e5",
                                "sense_id": "7d2ab731-0706-3b39-9848-b03d31064ca1",
                                "text": "On met les verjus & les moindres raisins au couchant & au nord, & les chasselas & les muscats, le long des murs, à l’exposition du midi ou du levant, lorsque le soleil y donne jusqu’à onze heures ou midi, afin qu’ils puissent mûrir."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07beea9a-68d9-4d6d-94d8-ea65c462dc90",
                                "sense_id": "7d2ab731-0706-3b39-9848-b03d31064ca1",
                                "text": "Par contre, les larves se développent plus vite sur les verjus que sur les grappes normales; poids de 100 larves, le même jour, 241 milligrammes sur les verjus et 42 milligrammes sur les grappes normales."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebe6f165-cf8c-4152-a03b-1fc23f4c525b",
                                "sense_id": "7d2ab731-0706-3b39-9848-b03d31064ca1",
                                "text": "Voici quatre mille ans que l’homme vendange à la main, il ne lui serait pas venu à l’esprit de couper les verjus, de maltraiter le raisin et blesser les ceps ainsi, surtout de ne pas couper la pourriture grise, alors que la machine, elle, prend tout."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d631b6c4-5643-4f43-a7a2-beece64222cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "e084e818-dbc5-32dc-a2ad-eeaae604e007",
                        "target_lang_word": "Verjus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5f502a21-2d72-4c7d-9d90-b3b893e1804c",
                        "source_entry_id": "e084e818-dbc5-32dc-a2ad-eeaae604e007",
                        "target_lang_word": "verjuice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verjuice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f793fbbd-7af8-3cc0-8bb2-4dcb39c4bf4e",
                                        "entry_id": "dfffa057-4e44-38f4-84a6-c56a6a0e4cb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A very acidic juice made by pressing unripe grapes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92b79b0a-d218-4d21-9300-a5baceb79549",
                                                "sense_id": "f793fbbd-7af8-3cc0-8bb2-4dcb39c4bf4e",
                                                "text": "In this inſtance, there is (vpon the by) to be noted the Percolation, or Suing of the Veriuyce thorow the VVood; So as it ſeemeth, it muſt be firſt in a kinde of Vapour, before it paſſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4664757c-812f-46cb-8671-a8d49ac1eb6f",
                                                "sense_id": "f793fbbd-7af8-3cc0-8bb2-4dcb39c4bf4e",
                                                "text": "Alfred pulled a face as of one that drinketh verjuice unawares; but let it pass: hypercriticism was not his cue just then."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05929a58-d9d7-4818-827d-b09048198bbf",
                                                "sense_id": "f793fbbd-7af8-3cc0-8bb2-4dcb39c4bf4e",
                                                "text": "She looked sour as verjuice when my mother and Emily entered, and gave them to understand that ‘she wasn’t used to no strangers in her school, and didn’t want ’em.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "verjuice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e701117-2d4e-31ac-8107-a0803da7f3ed",
                                        "entry_id": "a3e12a9e-db99-38a7-b785-2041bab2f7f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To render something sour; to embitter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ad61ccd-8b90-4034-bb86-cff44fa2c176",
                                                "sense_id": "2e701117-2d4e-31ac-8107-a0803da7f3ed",
                                                "text": "There are few names to which a jingle or a joke cannot be fitted—witness, Twining, banker and tea-dealer: / ‘Twining would be whining / Were’t not for his tea;’ / and the ex-Lord Mayor, Sir John Key, where the inherent rhyme to ‘donkey’ verjuiced the baronetcy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
